Subject: [PATCH] core: Fire Emblem Fates randomizer: chest and village items
 (the chest hook at ev::ItemGain)

Round 71 (docs/ROUND71_PLAN.md A1, docs/rando/CHESTS.md section 3, owner OK
"Yes, start round 71"): new module fates_rando_chests. What a chest, a village
or a talk gift gives is a literal IID in each chapter's event script, handed to
the script call ev::ItemGain = anonymous_namespace::ItemGain at 0x003B0768
(registration literal pool 0x0042B62C; r2 = the IID string at its entry; first
word push {r3-r7, lr} = 0xE92D40F8, read from the owner's dump).

While a randomized run whose folder holds a chest list (chests.txt, written by
rando.py make with --chests on; make_run_inner keeps it with the run like
plan.json) is active, the frame hook writes a reserved svc (0xEFFEC001; number
0xFEC001, above every kernel call) over that first word with
write32_privileged and has the recompiled code checked again
(recompiled::Library::check, as cheats.rs does for a cheat that changes code),
so the interpreter runs that one function. kernel::svc::dispatch hands the svc
to fates_rando_chests::on_svc: at 0x003B0768 only (ARM, the cpu past the svc)
it reads the IID r2 points at, finds (chapter, IID) in the list, where the
chapter is the placement file the game holds (map::Dispos name) and, when
readable, GameUserData's current chapter (CID_xxxx after its prefix) agrees,
checks that the new IID's own label text is at GameData's data start + the
listed offset, and points r2 at it; then it stores r3-r7 and lr below sp as
the replaced push did and the function goes on at +4 unchanged (window, sound,
convoy rule as for any gift). Any other svc 0xFEC001 is unknown as before.
No guest memory is allocated and no script byte is written.

Off = the original game: no list (the row off, the default; a run made
before round 71), no run, or a list with no changed item, and the word is
never written; the only thing the hook does then is read that one word once a
frame through the plain page read. When the list's run ends (a
non-randomized save, another run) the original word goes back at the next
frame; a save state holding the svc is put right the same way; the recompiled
code is checked again only when that word differs from what it was last
checked against (never, with the row off). A word that is neither the
original's nor ours (another game version, a cheat) is left alone; recompiled
code from an older 3dsrecomp that cannot tell a changed function keeps the
hook off.

Chest list: "fates-rando-chests 1", "seed <seed>", "c <chapter> <original IID
hex> <new IID hex> <new IID offset hex>" lines, "end <count>"; labels as the
bytes the game holds (cp932), the offset from GameData's data start (the base
of patch.txt's "g" label offsets); a missing end line or any unknown line
refuses the whole file (a notice; chests give their original items).

Tests: the_list_is_read_whole_or_refused, no_file_means_off,
the_word_follows_the_list_and_leaves_a_stranger_alone,
the_replaced_push_stores_r3_to_r7_and_lr,
a_listed_gift_of_the_chapter_being_played_is_swapped,
another_chapter_or_a_disagreeing_game_leaves_the_gift,
a_label_that_is_not_where_the_list_says_gives_the_original, chapter_keys
(cargo tests run in the gate / B3, not by the track). The Python twin
(tools/randomizer/chests.py parse_engine_list) reads the same test list.
